# Transform — cleaning, conforming, deduping

## Raw data → warehouse-ready

## The core operations

- **Clean** — nulls, bad types, invalid values; standardise dates/currency/casing
- **Conform** — map source codes to shared values (`'M'`/`'Male'`/`'1'` → `Male`)
- **Deduplicate** — same customer from web+POS+ERP → **one** row
- **Derive** — compute measures (`line_total`), apply business rules
- **Integrate** — join & merge cleaned sources into unified rows

## The single version of truth

- Data quality & consistency are **won or lost here**
- Conform + dedupe many sources → one trustworthy picture

## ETL vs ELT

- ETL: in the engine, before load · ELT: **SQL in-warehouse** (e.g. dbt)
